    <bpmn:process id="W_W3739" name="W3739. Energy Efficiency Officer, Energy Manager &amp; Energy Team Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Designation (W3738); organizational change
Frequency: Maintained + on change
Volume: EEO/Energy Manager/Energy Team
Owner: EEO / Sustainability
Participants: EEO, Sustainability (links to VS-25), Facilities (links to VS-20.3), Store Ops (links to VS-07), HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), Procurement (links to VS-34), Finance (links to VS-17.4), Renewable (links to VS-108)
Source: workflow W3739 — Energy Efficiency Officer, Energy Manager &amp; Energy Team Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3739_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3739_Lane1" name="EEO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3739_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3739_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3739_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3739_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3739_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3739_Start3" name="Designation (W3738); organizational change">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3739_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3739_Task4" name="EEO/Sustainability/HR establish and maintain the energy-management…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: EEO/Sustainability/HR establish and maintain the energy-management organization: the EEO (statutorily designated under RA 11285), the Energy Manager (operational), and the cross-functional Energy Team (Facilities, Store Ops, Procurement, Finance, Sustainability); manage roles, competencies, and RA 11285-required qualifications
Responsible (R): EEO / HR / Sustainability
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3739_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3739_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3739_Task5" name="EEO/Sustainability manage energy-management competency and capacity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: EEO/Sustainability manage energy-management competency and capacity: training/certification of the EEO/Energy Manager (links to VS-19.4), site-level energy champions at stores/DCs, and the energy-team operating cadence
Responsible (R): EEO / HR / Store Ops
Accountable (A): EEO
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3739_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3739_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3739_Task6" name="EEO/Sustainability integrate the energy team to operations: ensure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: EEO/Sustainability integrate the energy team to operations: ensure facility/store teams execute energy SOPs, energy considerations are embedded in facility/store operations (links to VS-20.3/VS-07), and the team reports to governance (links to W3737)
Responsible (R): EEO / Facilities / Store Ops
Accountable (A): EEO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3739_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3739_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3739_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3739_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3739_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-589 (ensure controlled execution — EEC Program Strategy, Designated-Establishment &amp; Governance (PA-120.1).) | - operational: training/certification; operational: qualification; operational: site-level champions
Owner: EEO / Sustainability</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
